Lumr Studio uses two models made by other people. It doesn't include them.
It downloads them on your say-so, from the hosts named below, into your own
cache folders. Their licenses are theirs, and this file is where the credit
lives. The plugin's own license is in LICENSE, and this file doesn't change it.

Speech recognition: NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2, CC-BY-4.0
  Made by NVIDIA.
  Model card: https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2
  License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Lumr Studio downloads the MLX conversion made by the mlx-community, at one
  pinned commit: https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2
  The conversion is a change to the original model. The plugin doesn't
  change it further.

Word timing: wav2vec 2.0 base 960h via torchaudio, MIT
  Made by the authors of wav2vec 2.0 (Baevski, Zhou, Mohamed and Auli, Meta AI),
  published in fairseq and redistributed by torchaudio under the same license.
  torchaudio's entry: https://docs.pytorch.org/audio/stable/generated/torchaudio.pipelines.WAV2VEC2_ASR_BASE_960H.html
  Source: https://github.com/facebookresearch/fairseq/tree/main/examples/wav2vec
